Subject: keep capturing when a cast starts with every buffer held

A consumer that pauses and resumes the stream as it starts, as `pipewiresrc`
does on its way to PLAYING, hands the stream back to the STREAMING state while
it still holds the buffers. The STREAMING handler dequeues once, finds none and
starts a capture with no buffer, which returns; the capture timer armed by the
first STREAMING fires on the buffer the pause re-queued and returns the same
way. The stream is its own driver, so nothing calls `process` again: the cast
delivers at most one frame and `kdos-record` writes a file with no picture in
it.

The STREAMING handler now arms the same retry timer the process handler uses
when it finds no buffer, a capture timed for a buffer that went back asks the
stream for another, and a capture that fires while one is in flight leaves the
in-flight frame to ask for the next.

--- a/src/screencast/ext_image_copy.c
+++ b/src/screencast/ext_image_copy.c
@@ -313,8 +313,20 @@

 void xdpw_ext_ic_frame_capture(struct xdpw_screencast_instance *cast) {
 	logprint(TRACE, "ext: start screencopy");
+	if (cast->ext_session.frame) {
+		// A capture is already in flight; its ready event asks the
+		// stream for the next buffer.
+		logprint(TRACE, "ext: frame already in flight");
+		return;
+	}
 	if (cast->current_frame.xdpw_buffer == NULL) {
-		logprint(ERROR, "ext: started frame without buffer");
+		// The buffer this capture was timed for went back to the
+		// stream (a pause re-queues it). Ask the stream for another,
+		// or nothing ever captures again.
+		logprint(DEBUG, "ext: no buffer for this frame, asking the stream");
+		if (cast->pwr_stream_state) {
+			pw_stream_trigger_process(cast->stream);
+		}
 		return;
 	}

